"Berners Lee said, ""He and his team don't talk to Facebook and Google about whether or not to introduce a complete change that will completely subdue all of their business models overnight."""
"We don't ask their permission."
In a post published in the medium on Saturday, Berners Lee wrote, "The mission of Intempt is to provide commercial energy and an ecosystem to help preserve the integrity and quality of the new web made in Solid."
In 1994, Berners-Lee developed the Internet when the World Wide Web Consortium was established at Massachusetts Institute of Technology.
In recent months, Berners-Lee was impacted by net neutrality debate.
Berners-Lee will continue to be the founder and director of the World Wi-Web Consortium, Web Foundation and Open Data Institute.
“I am incredibly optiminarisfied in this next era of the web,” Berners-Lee added.
